WEBVTT

01:29.940 --> 01:34.940
"The Basement"

01:35.572 --> 01:38.772
Sync and corrections by masaca
- addic7ed.com -

01:41.620 --> 01:42.870
Armin! Get down!

01:54.000 --> 01:54.920
It hurts...

01:55.880 --> 01:57.250
It hurts so bad...

02:28.120 --> 02:29.530
Bertholdt...

02:32.460 --> 02:33.290
It hurts...

02:36.460 --> 02:38.300
It hurts so bad...

02:38.550 --> 02:39.720
Sasha?

02:40.930 --> 02:42.050
Sasha!

02:42.510 --> 02:45.810
You're in terrible shape...
What happened...?

02:46.600 --> 02:47.390
Armin!

02:49.940 --> 02:50.770
Eren?

02:57.990 --> 03:00.320
I'm glad... you're back!

03:02.530 --> 03:03.600
Huh?

03:06.700 --> 03:07.680
You're up?

03:09.290 --> 03:10.440
Captain!

03:11.620 --> 03:14.730
What in the world happened here?

03:15.500 --> 03:18.570
I remember... Bertholdt becoming a Titan...

03:19.590 --> 03:22.550
What about the others?! Are they okay?!

03:23.510 --> 03:25.970
That's as far back as you remember?

03:26.430 --> 03:27.180
Huh?

03:27.770 --> 03:30.090
Eren, tell him everything.

03:52.000 --> 03:54.710
Well? Up to speed, Armin?

03:58.550 --> 04:01.800
Are you telling me... the Scout Regiment...

04:02.260 --> 04:05.840
...is the nine of us here... and that's it?

04:06.260 --> 04:07.760
For the time being.

04:08.220 --> 04:10.290
The fighting ended four hours ago.

04:10.600 --> 04:13.700
We've been looking for survivors,
but... none yet...

04:16.230 --> 04:21.240
S-So, we managed to seal
the walls of Shiganshina...

04:22.070 --> 04:25.650
But Reiner, the Beast Titan,
and one other escaped...

04:26.370 --> 04:28.240
Bertholdt was captured...

04:28.950 --> 04:32.539
Then... there was a dispute...

04:32.540 --> 04:35.250
...about using the injection on
Commander Erwin or me...

04:36.580 --> 04:37.450
And I...

04:38.420 --> 04:42.750
...turned into a Titan
and ate B-Bertholdt...

04:48.430 --> 04:49.300
Here.

05:04.900 --> 05:07.700
Why... did you pick me?

05:09.160 --> 05:11.369
No matter how you look at it,

05:11.370 --> 05:14.250
wasn't Commander Erwin
the right one to bring back?

05:15.160 --> 05:18.330
Captain! Why did you
give me the injection?!

05:18.920 --> 05:19.570
Tsk!

05:21.000 --> 05:22.960
I told you to tell him everything.

05:23.710 --> 05:28.290
The thing is, it seems your two
friends here didn't think that way.

05:29.010 --> 05:33.019
They stood up to me...
prepared to draw blood.

05:33.020 --> 05:33.810
Huh?

05:34.220 --> 05:36.840
We'll take whatever punishment comes.

05:38.060 --> 05:41.000
You'll be disciplined for
insubordination, but...

05:41.520 --> 05:44.070
Does taking the punishment
allow you to do anything?

05:45.280 --> 05:46.020
No...

05:47.740 --> 05:48.620
However...

05:49.700 --> 05:52.380
The final decision to choose you was mine.

05:53.200 --> 05:53.860
No...

05:55.000 --> 05:58.410
I chose this to be the
place where Erwin dies.

06:02.800 --> 06:04.690
I don't understand...

06:05.260 --> 06:08.020
There's no way it's
okay to let Erwin die...

06:08.840 --> 06:14.150
If the commander is gone,
how... how will we go on?

06:15.810 --> 06:19.810
I agree. I thought it should've
been used on Erwin...

06:20.310 --> 06:21.770
...if we're being brutally honest.

06:23.020 --> 06:26.800
No... It's a shame we were
put in that position...

06:30.240 --> 06:34.160
Anyways, Erwin entrusted Levi
with the decision to use it.

06:34.740 --> 06:36.980
And Levi ended up choosing you.

06:37.620 --> 06:39.210
There's nothing more to say.

06:40.080 --> 06:43.780
Erwin's life and a Titan's power
rest on your shoulders.

06:44.590 --> 06:49.930
No matter what anyone says,
that's part of who you are now, Armin.

06:53.550 --> 06:58.480
Does that mean... I need to be...
Erwin's replacement?

06:59.390 --> 07:01.840
No way... I can't...

07:04.820 --> 07:06.360
Don't get me wrong.

07:07.070 --> 07:09.330
You'll never be Erwin's replacement.

07:10.950 --> 07:11.810
But...

07:12.450 --> 07:16.570
...I know you have a strength
that nobody else has but you.

07:18.410 --> 07:20.640
I won't regret my decision.

07:21.330 --> 07:24.500
However, don't make these guys regret it.

07:25.380 --> 07:26.500
Nor anyone else.

07:28.510 --> 07:30.770
And don't regret it yourself, either.

07:32.220 --> 07:33.970
That is your mission.

07:42.520 --> 07:43.480
Shut up!

07:53.990 --> 07:56.190
We're no match for Sasha.

07:56.830 --> 08:01.459
Well, being the successor of Erwin
as commander of the Scouts,

08:01.460 --> 08:03.340
we're kinda in the same boat.

08:04.210 --> 08:07.000
From here on out,
we'll have to grin and bear it.

08:09.000 --> 08:09.960
Right...

08:11.510 --> 08:12.630
Now then...

08:13.260 --> 08:16.260
If it's not a problem for Armin,
we should get going.

08:17.390 --> 08:20.890
Levi, Eren, Mikasa, and
I will go investigate.

08:21.430 --> 08:25.399
You other four keep watch
from atop Shiganshina's wall.

08:25.400 --> 08:26.030
Roger.

08:26.900 --> 08:29.730
Eren. Do you still have the key?

08:31.400 --> 08:32.160
Yeah.

08:34.530 --> 08:35.310
Right here.

08:37.490 --> 08:38.270
Eren...

08:38.870 --> 08:39.920
When I get back,

08:40.330 --> 08:43.450
I'll show you the basement that
I've kept secret all this time.

08:44.710 --> 08:45.420
Hey, Eren!

08:46.380 --> 08:49.140
How many times must I say
you can't go in the basement?!

08:49.420 --> 08:51.200
Why aren't I allowed to?!

08:51.550 --> 08:54.379
Because your father keeps
his work tools there.

08:54.380 --> 08:55.340
Medicine, too.

08:55.970 --> 08:57.610
It's dangerous for children.

08:59.640 --> 09:00.530
Tsk...

09:10.110 --> 09:11.480
Your intentions are the key.

09:12.860 --> 09:16.410
The key to saving humankind
from this despair.

09:17.240 --> 09:20.080
We have reason to believe that the
basement of his home in Shiganshina...

09:20.530 --> 09:23.130
...houses a secret of the Titans
that not even he is aware of.

09:23.870 --> 09:28.379
If we can just reach this basement,
we may be able to obtain information

09:28.380 --> 09:33.260
that will help us break free from
the Titans' century-long tyranny.

10:02.410 --> 10:04.699
Hey, where's your house?

10:04.700 --> 10:06.000
R-Right...

11:59.440 --> 12:00.690
Is this it?

12:24.680 --> 12:25.510
Hey, Dad!

12:26.050 --> 12:28.340
When will you show me
what's in the basement?

12:28.970 --> 12:29.970
Who knows?

12:30.890 --> 12:34.510
Perhaps when you realize
the most important thing of all.

12:56.880 --> 13:00.340
Luckily, the fires didn't make it this far.

13:21.610 --> 13:22.320
Right here.

13:22.990 --> 13:25.310
Under this are the stairs to the basement.

13:25.650 --> 13:26.570
Good.

13:49.800 --> 13:52.930
That's a relief.
It's not flooded with water.

13:54.930 --> 13:55.870
Let's go.

14:16.410 --> 14:17.050
Eren.

14:18.330 --> 14:19.070
Right.

14:29.470 --> 14:30.230
What's wrong?

14:30.840 --> 14:31.470
Eren?

14:31.890 --> 14:32.890
Hurry it up.

14:35.220 --> 14:39.520
This... This key...
It doesn't go to this door...

14:39.980 --> 14:40.730
What?

14:41.310 --> 14:45.550
You're kidding... I'm certain that's
the key Dr. Jaeger had.

14:46.030 --> 14:47.319
Step aside.

14:47.320 --> 14:48.399
I'll open it.

14:48.400 --> 14:49.780
Huh? Wait...

14:53.740 --> 14:55.010
Hold up...

15:15.760 --> 15:19.139
It almost feels like a
laboratory down here.

15:19.140 --> 15:24.060
My dad was a doctor, so... he was always
cooped up down here mixing medicine.

15:24.520 --> 15:26.070
That makes sense.

15:27.400 --> 15:30.990
In fact, if this medicine
is all labeled correctly,

15:31.015 --> 15:34.409
it's stuff that's
widely available.

15:34.410 --> 15:36.829
And since all the books
here relate to medicine,

15:36.854 --> 15:39.144
at first glance,
it's just a doctor's study.

15:39.710 --> 15:42.190
"There's nothing suspicious here."

15:42.580 --> 15:45.130
It's like that's what he
wants people to think.

15:45.460 --> 15:46.190
Yeah...

15:46.750 --> 15:49.425
If you're hiding stuff
from the Interior Police,

15:49.450 --> 15:51.644
you wouldn't want
it out in the open.

15:53.720 --> 15:56.390
Hey. Quit standing around, brats.

15:56.680 --> 15:58.790
Erwin's hunches are rarely wrong.

15:59.890 --> 16:00.470
Right.

16:20.750 --> 16:23.900
Thanks, Mikasa. It's another all-nighter.

16:30.670 --> 16:31.550
Eren...

16:33.380 --> 16:35.340
There's a keyhole right here.

16:41.560 --> 16:42.120
Eren.

16:48.730 --> 16:49.620
It opened.

16:56.120 --> 16:57.369
It's empty?!

16:57.370 --> 16:58.370
Look closer.

17:00.080 --> 17:01.220
It's a false bottom.

17:07.420 --> 17:09.980
It smells like peppermint oil and charcoal.

17:10.590 --> 17:13.550
Were these treated to keep
moisture and bugs away?

17:14.010 --> 17:16.010
We were looking for something...

17:16.590 --> 17:17.660
and these must be it.

17:26.230 --> 17:30.090
I wonder what it was
my dad wanted to show me.

17:53.130 --> 17:56.510
That's when Erwin asked this question...

17:57.510 --> 18:02.290
"How do we know there's not
more humans outside the walls?"

18:03.520 --> 18:08.099
He insisted that as long as we haven't
been able to freely explore the outside,

18:08.100 --> 18:13.030
we can't know for sure if humanity
was completely wiped out by Titans.

18:13.780 --> 18:17.659
And yet, history books declare
the rest were wiped out.

18:17.660 --> 18:18.260
Hmm?

18:18.740 --> 18:22.290
If you consider that history books
should maintain an objective viewpoint,

18:22.620 --> 18:26.280
it should read, "It is believed
the rest of humanity was wiped out."

18:26.790 --> 18:30.129
You're just trying to find fault
in anything and everything.

18:30.130 --> 18:33.090
I'm not! There's intent behind it!

18:33.630 --> 18:34.799
For example...

18:34.800 --> 18:38.620
To make us believe that humanity
doesn't exist outside the walls.

18:39.090 --> 18:43.170
That is, by the royal government
that issues the books.

18:43.970 --> 18:45.510
You're overthinking it.

18:45.930 --> 18:48.330
This is what they call splitting hairs.

18:50.150 --> 18:53.520
I was teasing him back then,
but look at us now...

18:54.070 --> 18:57.010
You'll just have to apologize
to the man himself.

19:00.240 --> 19:02.790
In not too long, it'll be dawn.

19:03.530 --> 19:06.490
If our heroes were to return,
it's about that time...

19:08.000 --> 19:10.790
The Scouts returned just a moment ago!

19:11.500 --> 19:14.050
They successfully took back Wall Maria!

19:37.110 --> 19:39.430
This is... a portrait?

19:40.700 --> 19:41.770
Let me see that.

19:43.490 --> 19:48.040
No... It's far too detailed for this
to be drawn by a person.

19:48.370 --> 19:50.380
That's Dr. Jaeger's writing.

19:52.370 --> 19:54.140
"This is no illustration.

19:54.540 --> 19:58.299
Instead, this uses light
reflected off a subject...

19:58.300 --> 20:01.300
...and burns the image on special paper.

20:01.510 --> 20:03.360
It's called a photograph.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.179
I come from a place outside"...

20:06.180 --> 20:08.980
...the walls where humanity
lives in elegance.

20:10.730 --> 20:13.200
Humanity has not perished.

20:13.940 --> 20:18.490
I pray the person who finds
this book is a fellow patriot.

21:38.810 --> 21:41.939
Hurry, Fay!
We'll lose it unless we're fast!

21:41.940 --> 21:43.630
Wait up, Grisha!

21:44.240 --> 21:46.320
You two stop right there.

21:47.610 --> 21:51.250
I told you not to forget
your armbands when you go outside.

21:51.910 --> 21:55.709
Grisha, you absolutely
must not leave the walls.

21:55.710 --> 21:56.830
Hey, wait!

21:58.420 --> 21:59.999
I got it, Mom!

22:00.000 --> 22:01.630
We'll be back!

22:02.960 --> 22:03.620
Come on!

22:11.430 --> 22:15.540
When I first thought as to how
I should start my story...

22:16.190 --> 22:18.170
...I immediately thought of that day.

22:18.650 --> 22:19.760
Hey!

22:20.690 --> 22:22.069
...Whoa!
...Sorry!

22:22.070 --> 22:24.900
Grisha, be careful!
Watch where you're going!

22:27.990 --> 22:30.030
Oh... It's leaving...

22:31.700 --> 22:32.880
Must be nice...

22:33.160 --> 22:37.750
Someday when I'm rich, will I be able
to ride on an airship, too?

22:39.170 --> 22:43.420
What are you talking about?
There's no way either of us will get rich.

22:44.050 --> 22:44.680
Yeah...

22:45.340 --> 22:46.670
But it must be nice...

22:47.550 --> 22:49.760
I wonder what we could see from up there.

22:55.720 --> 22:56.860
There it goes...

23:11.410 --> 23:12.489
Let's go, Fay!

23:12.490 --> 23:13.579
Huh?!

23:13.580 --> 23:17.709
My teacher said the airships take off
and land at a place near here!

23:17.710 --> 23:18.500
Let's go see!

23:18.960 --> 23:22.380
What?! But Mom said we're
not allowed to leave the walls!

23:22.670 --> 23:24.960
It'll be fine! Just for a bit!

23:25.090 --> 23:25.840
...We'll be right back!

23:25.841 --> 23:27.970
...Hey! Get back here!
...We'll be right back!

23:28.880 --> 23:30.520
That naive day of my youth...

23:31.180 --> 23:32.060
...when I...

23:32.890 --> 23:35.410
...had to face the truth of this world.

23:35.682 --> 23:38.882
Sync and corrections by masaca
- addic7ed.com -

23:40.560 --> 23:46.530
His story began with pulling his sister's
hand while gazing upwards at the sky.

23:47.150 --> 23:52.360
The hatred and hope reflected in
his eyes show Eren a cruel world.

23:52.990 --> 23:54.880
Next episode: "That Day."

23:54.881 --> 23:56.539
"That Day"
